{"step_index":345,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T07:22:13Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Payment Simulation Failure**\n\nI've examined the screenshot and decoded the email address. It appears \"info@morganzintec.ac.zw\" is the target. Clicking the \"Simulate Successful Payment\" button produces a persistent \"❌ Not Found\" status. This suggests the simulation is not correctly linking the provided email address to a successful payment state, regardless of the simulated trigger.\n\n\n**Investigating Vercel Function Routing**\n\nI'm now exploring how Vercel routes requests within serverless functions. My attention is on the 404 error returned by `POST /api/demo-payment`. Specifically, I am testing Vercel's zero-config multi-file routing approach, and I've created dedicated Python files in the api/ directory to test. I'm trying to see if they'll pick up the requests correctly. I'm also considering `api/index.py` with a root wildcard.\n\n\n**Tracing Path Handling**\n\nI'm now focusing on how FastAPI interacts with Vercel's routing, specifically the path variations. I'm considering all possibilities: `/api/demo-payment`, `/demo-payment`, `/api/index/demo-payment`, and so on. My focus is now on implementing decorators or middleware to normalize and handle these different path prefixes, essentially making `request.scope[\"path\"]` equal to `/api/demo-payment` regardless of how the request is received. I'm going to inspect the raw incoming path to debug what's happening. I'm also planning to inspect how FastAPI's middleware can be used to rewrite the request path.\n\n\n**Implementing Path Normalization**\n\nI've crafted a robust middleware to normalize incoming paths. It intercepts requests before FastAPI's routing and examines the raw path.  Based on the presence of keywords like \"demo-payment,\" \"play-events,\" or \"media,\" I'm dynamically updating `request.scope[\"path\"]` to a standardized form. This ensures FastAPI consistently matches the correct routes, eliminating 404 errors regardless of how Vercel initially routes the request.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\\\app.py\"","EndLine":"275","StartLine":"245","toolAction":"\"Viewing middleware in app.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Viewing middleware in app.py\""}}]}
{"step_index":346,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T07:22:33Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-26T09:22:33+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-26T09:22:33+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py`\nTotal Lines: 562\nTotal Bytes: 20608\nShowing lines 245 to 275\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n245: # --- FastAPI Application ---\n246: \n247: app = FastAPI(\n248:     title=\"StreamWave Serverless Media Platform API\",\n249:     description=\"FastAPI Backend for StreamWave Entertainment with Academic Payment Simulation & Session Access Control\",\n250:     version=\"2.1.0\",\n251:     docs_url=\"/docs\",\n252:     redoc_url=\"/redoc\",\n253: )\n254: \n255: \n256: # Security Response Headers Middleware\n257: @app.middleware(\"http\")\n258: async def add_security_headers(request: Request, call_next):\n259:     response = await call_next(request)\n260:     response.headers[\"X-Content-Type-Options\"] = \"nosniff\"\n261:     response.headers[\"X-Frame-Options\"] = \"DENY\"\n262:     response.headers[\"X-XSS-Protection\"] = \"1; mode=block\"\n263:     response.headers[\"Referrer-Policy\"] = \"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"\n264:     return response\n265: \n266: \n267: # --- Public HTML Page Routes ---\n268: \n269: @app.get(\"/\", response_class=FileResponse, include_in_schema=False)\n270: async def serve_landing_page():\n271:     \"\"\"Serves the public StreamWave landing page.\"\"\"\n272:     landing_file = PUBLIC_DIR / \"index.html\"\n273:     if landing_file.exists():\n274:         return FileResponse(str(landing_file))\n275:     raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=\"Landing page not found\")\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":347,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-26T07:22:34Z","thinking":"**Implementing Path Normalization**\n\nI've begun implementing the `normalize_api_path` middleware within `app.py`. This is to enhance Vercel Serverless Function routing. It will act as an HTTP middleware, taking a `request` and passing it to `call_next`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import base64\\nimport hashlib\\nimport hmac\\nimport json\\nimport logging\\nimport os\\nimport shutil\\nimport time\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import List, Optional\\n\\nfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, HTTPException, Path as PathParam, Query, Request, Response, status\\nfrom fastapi.responses import FileResponse\\nfrom fastapi.staticfiles import StaticFiles\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\\n\\n# Configure structured Python logger\\nlogging.basicConfig(\\n    level=logging.INFO, format=\\\"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(name)s: %(message)s\\\"\\n)\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\\\"streamwave\\\")\\n\\nBASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nDATA_FILE = BASE_DIR / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"media.json\\\"\\nPUBLIC_DIR = BASE_DIR / \\\"public\\\"\\nMEDIA_DIR = PUBLIC_DIR / \\\"media\\\"\\nIMAGES_DIR = PUBLIC_DIR / \\\"images\\\"\\n\\nPREVIEW_VIDEO_FILE = MEDIA_DIR / \\\"streamwave-preview.mp4\\\"\\nLOGO_IMAGE_FILE = IMAGES_DIR / \\\"streamwave-logo.png\\\"\\n\\n# Centralized Subscription Plan Configuration\\nSUBSCRIPTION_PLAN = {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"streamwave-monthly\\\",\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"StreamWave Monthly\\\",\\n    \\\"price\\\": \\\"US$2.99 per month\\\",\\n    \\\"price_amount\\\": 2.99,\\n    \\\"currency\\\": \\\"USD\\\",\\n    \\\"interval\\\": \\\"month\\\",\\n    \\\"benefits\\\": [\\n        \\\"Full Zimbabwean catalogue access\\\",\\n        \\\"5-second MP4 movie previews\\\",\\n        \\\"Demonstration music audio samples\\\",\\n        \\\"Access on desktop or mobile\\\",\\n    ],\\n}\\n\\n# Session Cookie Signing Secret (Read from environment variable, never hardcoded in production)\\nDEMO_SESSION_SECRET = os.getenv(\\n    \\\"DEMO_SESSION_SECRET\\\", \\\"streamwave-secret-key-academic-demo-2026\\\"\\n).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef create_session_token(email: str, expiry_seconds: int = 86400 * 7) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generates an HMAC-SHA256 signed session token for a paid demonstration member.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    payload = {\\n        \\\"email\\\": email.strip().lower(),\\n        \\\"plan_id\\\": SUBSCRIPTION_PLAN[\\\"id\\\"],\\n        \\\"exp\\\": int(time.time()) + expiry_seconds,\\n    }\\n    json_bytes \n<truncated 20864 bytes>","Description":"\"Add normalize_api_path ASGI middleware to app.py to dynamically rewrite incoming paths for API endpoints\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\\\app.py\"","toolAction":"\"Updating app.py with path normalization middleware\"","toolSummary":"\"Updating app.py with path normalization middleware\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
